<title>MONACO: TENNIS-LEADING ATP TOUR PRIZE-MONEY WINNERS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-LEADING ATP TOUR PRIZE-MONEY WINNERS.</headline>
<dateline>MONACO 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading prize-money winners issued</p>
<p>by the ATP Tour on Monday:</p>
<p> 1. Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia)	$1,863,713</p>
<p> 2. Pete Sampras (U.S.)		   1,754,922</p>
<p> 3. Thomas Muster (Austria)	     1,516,166</p>
<p> 4. Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia)	  1,424,105</p>
<p> 5. Michael Chang (U.S.)		  1,379,916</p>
<p> 6. Richard Krajicek (Netherlands)    1,190,281</p>
<p> 7. Andre Agassi (U.S.)		   1,045,660</p>
<p> 8. Todd Woodbridge (Australia)	   942,738</p>
<p> 9. Mark Woodforde (Australia)	    919,482</p>
<p> 10. Wayne Ferreira (South Africa)	909,390</p>
<p> 11. Boris Becker (Germany)		 849,827</p>
<p> 12. Marc Rosset (Switzerland)	    813,239</p>
<p> 13. Jakob Hlasek (Switzerland)	   807,128</p>
<p> 14. Alberto Costa (Spain)		  764,411</p>
<p> 15. Marcelo Rios (Chile)		   743,648</p>
